  "name": "Kapuka (Kenyan urban pop)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Kapuka Kenyan urban-pop genre emerging in early-2000s Nairobi from the Ogopa DJs and Calif Records production camps. Characterized by mid-tempo beat with Swahili-Sheng (Nairobi street-slang) and English lyrical content over R&B-influenced synthesizer-and-drum-machine production. Distinguished from parallel genge by kapuka's slower-tempo R&B-leaning (vs genge's faster-hardcore-hip-hop-leaning) aesthetic targeting middle-class urban-Nairobi commercial-radio. Producer Lucas Bikedo at Ogopa DJs formed the production-hub anchor.",
  "recipe": "classic East African 2000-2003 kapuka, functional Song, African pop branch, intl hip hop MC rhythm antilliaanse rap irish trap. equal tempered, solo with instrumental accompaniment. TR-808, analog synth, mid rich alder electric bass. dar es salaam zanzibar taarab culture club. tube condenser, 500-series boutique pre, brick-wall limiter, dynamic EQ. 24-bit digital plate reverb digital delay pitch shifter.",
